# Microsoft Entra ID Security Group Assignment Documentation

## Cedar Valley Health Zero Trust Identity Lab

## Objective

The objective of this task was to create Microsoft Entra ID security groups based on department responsibilities and assign users according to their business functions.

Security groups allow Cedar Valley Health to manage access efficiently by assigning permissions to groups instead of individual users.

This supports Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and the Principle of Least Privilege.

---

# Security Groups Created

## CVH-Executives

Executive leadership responsible for strategic planning, governance, organizational oversight, and executive decision-making.

---

## CVH-Finance-Team

Finance professionals responsible for accounting, payroll, budgeting, financial reporting, and revenue management.

---

## CVH-HR-Team

Human Resources personnel responsible for recruiting, onboarding, employee records, benefits administration, and workforce management.

---

## CVH-IT-Department

Information Technology professionals responsible for Identity and Access Management (IAM), cloud administration, technical support, infrastructure management, cybersecurity operations, and system maintenance.

---

## CVH-Sales-Team

Business Development and Community Outreach personnel responsible for expanding community partnerships, promoting healthcare services, coordinating employer wellness initiatives, and supporting organizational growth.

---

# RBAC Design Approach

Each security group was created to support Role-Based Access Control by assigning permissions according to business responsibilities rather than assigning permissions directly to individual users.

This approach:

- Simplifies administration
- Improves scalability
- Supports Least Privilege
- Reduces administrative overhead
- Creates consistent access management

